Falsifies `pci::verification::the_bus_queue_stays_inside_its_array_on_any_firmware`.

The defect: the already-seen check is deleted, so `enqueue` becomes idempotent in the bitmap
(`|=` is) but not in the queue. The line looks redundant beside a `|=` that is itself
idempotent, which is what makes deleting it the plausible error rather than a contrived one, and
it is the whole bound: nothing in `enqueue` checks `tail` against 256.

Expected to fail: the harness's first assertion, `q.tail == queued(&q.seen)`, whenever the bus
enqueued was already seen. That is the invariant the 256 bound is derived from, so under this
defect firmware that names one bus from several bridges walks `tail` past the end of a
256-element array.

diff --git a/crates/pci_configuration_space/src/lib.rs b/crates/pci_configuration_space/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/pci_configuration_space/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/pci_configuration_space/src/lib.rs
@@ -290,5 +290,2 @@ impl BusQueue {
         let (word, bit) = (bus as usize >> 6, 1u64 << (bus & 63));
-        if self.seen[word] & bit != 0 {
-            return;
-        }
         self.seen[word] |= bit;
